The reference decoders in t27/formats.t27 restate public storage layouts from
ggml-org/llama.cpp, PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp, microsoft/BitNet,
huggingface/transformers, ml-explore/mlx and microsoft/onnxruntime, and the
tensor-layout rules of huggingface/safetensors (Metadata::validate,
read_metadata, Dtype::bitsize); they are independent implementations, not
copies of that code. The contracts in specs/formats/*.t27 and the test oracle
in tools/generate-spec-vectors.py restate the same layouts and rules, citing
the pinned upstream commit and lines of each (specs/formats/upstream.lock.json).
Those upstream projects are licensed by their authors: llama.cpp and its
PrismML and bitnet.cpp forks, microsoft/BitNet, ml-explore/mlx and
microsoft/onnxruntime under the MIT License; huggingface/transformers and
huggingface/safetensors under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
